### =========================================================================
### 🎓 AUDIT LOG — sino, ano, kanino, saan, kailan
### 📅 Day 48 · Phase 10 (Roles at admin)
### =========================================================================
### Itinatala sa table na audit_logs (hindi sa Pino logs — iyon ay para sa debugging):
###   register · login · login_failed · logout · access_denied (403) · admin_list_users · admin_list_audit_logs
###
### Bawat row: action · actorId (sino ang gumawa) · targetId (ang naapektuhan) · ip (totoong IP) ·
###            userAgent · metadata · createdAt
### 🔐 Kailanman: walang password, token, o cookie sa audit log.
###
### Kailangan: dev admin (palitan ang password sa #3) — tingnan ang 13-admin-rbac.http
### Code: backend/src/lib/audit.ts · backend/src/routes/admin.ts (listAuditLogs)
### Test: backend/src/lib/audit.test.ts · Diagram: docs/diagrams/02-er-diagram.md
### =========================================================================

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Maling password sa sarili mong admin account. Ang inaasahan:
###    401 — at isang row: login_failed · actorId: null (hindi pa kilala) · targetId: <id mo> ·
###    metadata: { "email": "..." } — ang tinype na email, HINDI ang password
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nelson_dev@1869.com",
  "password": "mali-muna-ito"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Email na walang account. Ang inaasahan: 401 — row: login_failed · targetId: null
###    🔍 Pareho ang oras ng #1 at #2 (sinukat Day 48: median 85ms vs 81ms) — itinatala ang dalawa
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "walang-ganito@example.com",
  "password": "mali-muna-ito"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Tamang login bilang admin. Ang inaasahan: 200 — row: login · actorId: <id mo>
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nelson_dev@1869.com",
  "password": "PALITAN-NG-PASSWORD-MO"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Tingnan ang audit log (pinakabago muna). Ang inaasahan:
###    200 { "logs": [ { "id", "action", "actorId", "actorEmail", "targetId", "ip", "userAgent",
###                      "metadata", "createdAt" }, ... ], "page": 1, "limit": 10, "total", "totalPages" }
###    Ang pinakabago: admin_list_audit_logs — pati ang pagtingin mo ay itinatala
###    Susunod: login (#3), login_failed (#2), login_failed (#1)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/audit-logs?limit=10

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Page 2 (pareho ng pagination ng Day 47)
### 🔍 Pansinin (sinubukan, Day 48): ang UNANG row ng page 2 ay kapareho ng HULING row ng page 1!
###    Ang pagtingin mo sa page 2 ay gumawa ng bagong row (admin_list_audit_logs), kaya umusog ang lahat
###    nang isa. Ito ang kahinaan ng offset pagination (Day 47) — ayos: cursor pagination (?before=<id>)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/audit-logs?page=2&limit=10

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Mag-logout. Ang inaasahan: 204 — row: logout · actorId: <id mo>
###    (Kahit walang valid na token, gumagana ang logout — actorId: null lang sa row)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/logout
